# P&L Variance Summary – FY2025

## YoY Performance (vs Prior Year Same Period)

**Critical Issues:**
- **Operating Profit & Net Profit flipped to loss.** Operating Profit declined RM 4.68M (–371%), swinging from RM 1.26M profit to RM 3.42M loss. Net Profit fell RM 3.34M (–242%), from RM 1.38M profit to RM 1.96M loss.
- **Gross Profit compressed 28%** (RM 5.63M vs RM 7.82M). Gross margin eroded 2.9 percentage points (6.9% vs 9.8%).
- **Cost of Sales outpaced revenue growth:** COGS up 5.3% (RM 3.82M) while Net Sales rose only 2.0% (RM 1.63M).
- **Operating Costs surged 38%** (RM 2.49M increase to RM 9.05M)—the largest unfavourable deviation after COGS.

**Partial Offset:**
- Other Income jumped RM 1.34M (+1,134%), mitigating losses but insufficient to restore profitability.

**Verdict:** Severe deterioration. Business moved from profitable to loss-making despite modest top-line growth.

---

## Budget Variance (vs Approved Budget)

**On Track.** Actual results match approved budget within rounding (all variances ≤ RM 4, <0.1%). No material deviations.

---

## Overall Picture

The business is **underperforming operationally** year-over-year due to margin compression and cost inflation, though budget execution is tight. The loss position was not anticipated in the prior year.

